ing and a tossup rating from several raters argue against widening the margin further.", "watch": "A second debate or a shift in the anti-Muslim rhetoric storyline could move late-deciding voters either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gary Peters (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open Senate seat pits Democrat Abdul El-Sayed against Republican Mike Rogers after Gary Peters' retirement. The state's partisan lean is even, making this a genuine battleground, though recent polling has consistently favored El-Sayed by roughly three to five points. Late October surveys from both partisan and independent pollsters show him narrowly ahead, and prediction markets give him about a two-in-three chance of winning.\n\nThe race has drawn heavy outside money, with super PACs spending far more against El-Sayed than Rogers has attracted, and the first debate drew national attention amid heated exchanges and anti-Muslim rhetoric. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean D or Tilt D, with a few calling it a tossup. The forecast expects a narrow Democratic win with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7427, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07